# The subcommand list is read from `codex --help` on the build you have — 26 of
# them at the last look, so the curated groups below come first and the full
# list goes at the bottom.
name:    codex
what:    OpenAI Codex CLI. Routed by ~/.codex/config.toml, key from the env
check:   codex
docs:    codex --help; codex doctor when something is off
probe:   help

= STARTING
codex            | new session here. Aliased to `cx`
codex resume --last | continue the most recent. Aliased to `cxr`
@codex resume    | pick an older session from a list. Aliased to `cxrr`
codex fork --last | branch off the last session instead of continuing it
@codex exec      | run once, non-interactively, and print the answer
codex -C DIR     | run as if you had cd'd to DIR first
codex --worktree | run in a fresh git worktree, leaving your tree alone

= THE THINGS ONLY CODEX HAS
@codex apply     | apply the diff it last produced, as a git apply
@codex review    | a code review, non-interactively
@codex queue     | queue a message for a session that is already running
@codex agents    | browse every session on the local daemon
@codex doctor    | check config, auth and runtime health in one go
@codex sandbox   | run a command inside codex's own sandbox

= SESSION HOUSEKEEPING
codex archive ID | put a session away without deleting it
codex unarchive ID | bring it back
codex delete ID  | permanently delete a saved session
@codex mcp       | manage its MCP servers
@codex plugin    | manage its plugins
@codex update    | update the binary

= WHICH POOL AM I USING
codex -m NAME    | one run against a different combo. NAME is a combo name
codex -p NAME    | use a [profiles.NAME] block from ~/.codex/config.toml
--strict-config  | fail loudly on a config key this build does not know.
                 | Use it after every edit to ~/.codex/config.toml
omniroute-where  | which gateway and which combo, from shell/common.sh

= APPROVALS AND SANDBOXING
-s, --sandbox    | read-only, workspace-write, or danger-full-access
-a, --ask-for-approval | untrusted, on-failure, on-request, never
--approve-for-me | stop asking and approve as it goes
--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox | no guard rails at all

= ALL FLAGS (from --help)
